commit message:
Use code generation for primitive math and array functions

Adds a maven plugin (chartfx-generate) to the source tree, which
generates variants for primitive types from template classes and adds
them to generate sources.

There are two types of template:

*GenBase classes are replaced by a class of the same name without the
suffix where all sections inside the following comment are repeated
substituting the given type
//// codegen: originalType -> outputType1, outputType2, ...
// example function
public originalType(originalType input1, int input2) {
    // you can skip lines from being replaced
    originalType foo; //// codegen: skip all
    originalType bar; //// codegen: skip outputType2
    // you can add substitutions for a special type
    // use any character instead of '%' that you dont need in your text
    // syntax: subst<sep><(list of) outputTypes><sep><search><sep><replace>
    foo = fn1(bar); //// codegen: subst%outputType2%fn1%fn2
    // use returncast to add a cast before return or assignment
    return someFunction(input1, input2, foo); //// codegen: returncast all
}
//// end codegen
// don't forget to end the section

*Proto classes will generate a separate class for each primitive type
which can be used to generalize data classes

(cherry picked from commit d838b3e7163e0dece242bb61a86fe45fefd3caea)

